<h2>{% trans %}Prepare your import{% endtrans %}</h2>
<ol>
  <li>{% trans %}Download the latest template or example spreadsheet from the import dashboard.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}Fill in the required columns. Mandatory columns are highlighted in the preflight checklist.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}Gather supporting files such as images referenced in the sheet and ensure they are reachable by the site.{% endtrans %}</li>
</ol>

<h2>{% trans %}Run the import wizard{% endtrans %}</h2>
<ol>
  <li>{% trans %}Navigate to <strong>Content → Blue Marloc Import</strong>.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}Upload your spreadsheet on the first panel and verify the detected headers.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}Use the preflight checks to confirm required vocabularies, paragraphs, and images are available.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}Start the batch process and monitor progress messages. You can pause or resume as needed.{% endtrans %}</li>
</ol>

<h2>{% trans %}After the import{% endtrans %}</h2>
<ul>
  <li>{% trans %}Review the summary messages for rows that were skipped or updated.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}Use the inspector panel to cross-check imported nodes against spreadsheet rows.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}If an error occurs, download the log output and share it with the development team for troubleshooting.{% endtrans %}</li>
</ul>
